 34CL    32S(3HE,PG)                   1973CA15,1971DE27,1971SN01ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  {+32}S+1p+1n|){+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+32}S ground state.                 
 34CL c  1973Ca15: 9.0-MeV {+3}He beam from the Utrecht 6 MV tandem Van de      
 34CL2c  Graaff generator on a natural Sb{-2}S{-3} target. Protons were detected
 34CL3c  using two Si surface-barrier detectors and |g rays were detected using 
 34CL4c  a Ge(Li) detector. Measured p|g-coin. Deduced lifetimes using DSAM.    
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1971De27: 8.0-9.0-MeV {+3}He beams from the Notre Dame model FN tandem 
 34CL2c  Van de Graaff accelerator on natural CdS targets. Protons were detected
 34CL3c  using an annular Si surface-barrier detector and |g rays were detected 
 34CL4c  using NaI(Tl) detectors and coaxial Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E{-p},  
 34CL5c  E|g, I|g, and p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios,
 34CL6c  and mixing ratios.                                                     
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1971Sn01: 6.8-MeV {+3}He beam from the Brookhaven National Laboratory  
 34CL2c  3.5-MeV Van de Graaff accelerator on a 95% {+32}S target. |g rays were 
 34CL3c  detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels and
 34CL4c  lifetimes using DSAM. Also measured {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl reaction at  
 34CL5c  the Stony Brook tandem Van de Graaff accelerator and deduced lifetimes 
 34CL6c  using RDM.                                                             
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Br11: 7.5-MeV {+3}He beam from the Utrecht 6-MV tandem Van de      
 34CL2c  Graaff generator on a natural ZnS target. Protons were detected using  
 34CL3c  two Si surface-barrier detectors and |g rays were detected using a     
 34CL4c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured p|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching
 34CL5c  ratios, and lifetimes using DSAM.                                      
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Br10: 5.2-MeV {+3}He beam from the Padova 5.5-MV Van de Graaff     
 34CL2c  generator on a natural CdS target. Protons were detected using an      
 34CL3c  annular Si surface-barrier detector and |g rays were detected using a  
 34CL4c  Ge(Li) detector and a NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and  
 34CL5c  p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios, and mixing   
 34CL6c  ratios. Also measured {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl reaction using a Ge(Li)    
 34CL7c  detector and deduced lifetimes using DSAM.                             
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Sy01: 5.75-MeV {+3}He beam from the University of Groningen Van de 
 34CL2c  Graaff accelerator on natural ZnS target. Protons were detected using a
 34CL3c  Si annular detector and |g rays were detected using a NaI(Tl) detector.
 34CL4c  Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced levels, J, |g-ray  
 34CL5c  branching ratios, and mixing ratios.                                   
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Th10: 9-, 9.5-, 10-MeV {+3}He beams on natural ZnS target at       
 34CL2c  Nuclear Research Institute, Strasbourg, France. Protons were detected  
 34CL3c  using a Si surface-barrier detector and |g rays were detected using a  
 34CL4c  NaI detector. Measured |gp(|q). Deduced levels and J.                  
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1972AlZT,1971AlZB: DSAM with 8.5-MeV {+3}He beam at University of Notre
 34CL2c  Dame.                                                                  
